From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:12:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/33] pipelined ExecIndirect3 on a FIFO (prototype, off
 unless REIMS_VGPU_PIPELINE_EXEC names an existing file)

A pipelining FIFO sends a remote task's exec and goes on; the reply's follow-up (backing
invalidation, failure completion) settles later on the FIFO thread in send order. The FIFO
event value is reserved at send; a refused/faulted exec commits a fill command buffer that
keeps the cross-task event chain moving, and the host signals after a crash.
Not for adoption.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
